Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: match SP11 CSID1 common lifecycle

Use the exact same-machine Windows CSID1 lifecycle for the bounded front
mode0 path. Program wrapper route 0x101 before reset, use software-only
RESET_CMD=2 with RESET_CFG=0x11 and TOP mask 1, then run the full Gen2
CSID builder immediately after reset. Do not stage the generic Linux
pre-reset IRQ_CMD clear or post-reset all-path masks on this front path.

Place each captured CSID 0x803 companion write after its matching IFE
startup packet, keep the existing 0x804 IPP enable order, and use the
Windows hardware-reset-only stop callback for private rollback. This also
avoids calling V4L2 s_stream(false) for a subdevice that the private
runner never started through V4L2.

Remove the old +0x328/+0x32c final-state replay because neither the exact
full builder nor the captured companion packets own those writes.

Generic/non-front CSID680 reset behavior is unchanged.

---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-680.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-680.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-680.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-680.c
